YUMI ICHINOSE SEX APPEAL

270
00:23:57,980 --> 00:24:00,938
IS YUMI ICHINOSE NOT HOT?
HERE'S WHAT WE FOUND

271
00:24:04,271 --> 00:24:06,021
PRETTY, BUT SOMEHOW DISAPPOINTING

272
00:24:06,105 --> 00:24:07,980
WHY YUMI ICHINOSE LACKS SEX APPEAL

273
00:24:08,063 --> 00:24:09,521
NEWS ANCHORS WHO LACK SEX APPEAL

274
00:24:14,646 --> 00:24:17,021
WHY ARE THERE NO DATING RUMORS
ABOUT YUMI ICHINOSE?

275
00:24:17,105 --> 00:24:20,271
YUMI ICHINOSE SHUN KAZUMA PERFECT MATCH

276
00:24:22,980 --> 00:24:24,646
KAZUMA
HERE'S THE RESTAURANT

277
00:24:27,313 --> 00:24:28,313
Oh, Ichinose.

278
00:24:30,105 --> 00:24:31,563
I just sent you the link.

279
00:24:31,646 --> 00:24:32,646
I got it.

280
00:24:32,730 --> 00:24:34,563
-You like sushi, right?
-Yes.

281
00:24:35,146 --> 00:24:37,438
Yay! High-end sushi.

282
00:24:38,938 --> 00:24:41,105
Hi, you two.

283
00:24:41,980 --> 00:24:43,813
-Hi.
-Hi.

284
00:24:50,146 --> 00:24:51,605
Is it okay if we meet there?

285
00:24:52,105 --> 00:24:54,146
I've got a meeting after the show.

286
00:24:54,646 --> 00:24:56,105
Of course. That's fine.

287
00:24:56,605 --> 00:24:57,605
See you then.

288
00:25:05,105 --> 00:25:06,105
Sushi.

289
00:25:08,313 --> 00:25:10,146
Thank you for meeting with me today.

290
00:25:10,980 --> 00:25:14,355
I wanted to talk to you in this world too,

291
00:25:14,438 --> 00:25:16,021
so I chose this avatar.

292
00:25:16,771 --> 00:25:18,605
No problem. Thank you.

293
00:25:19,105 --> 00:25:22,355
Regular visits to the clinic
started to become a bit of a hassle,

294
00:25:22,438 --> 00:25:23,938
so this really helps.

295
00:25:24,938 --> 00:25:26,605
I'm glad to hear that.

296
00:25:30,688 --> 00:25:34,646
The other day, you asked me
why I use this avatar, right?

297
00:25:35,355 --> 00:25:36,355
Yes.

298
00:25:37,146 --> 00:25:39,230
I gave it some thought.

299
00:25:41,563 --> 00:25:43,313
I think it's because…

300
00:25:46,938 --> 00:25:50,230
my real body feels more like
an avatar than this one does.

301
00:25:53,313 --> 00:25:56,146
I feel like I have to act like a CEO

302
00:25:57,230 --> 00:25:59,896
and dress appropriately.

303
00:26:02,688 --> 00:26:04,521
I wear expensive clothes,

304
00:26:05,188 --> 00:26:07,188
drive an expensive car,

305
00:26:07,271 --> 00:26:09,605
live in an expensive house,
and put on a brave face.

306
00:26:12,188 --> 00:26:13,188
But

307
00:26:15,563 --> 00:26:18,563
when I take this form,
I don't have to act tough.

308
00:26:21,021 --> 00:26:23,146
I can shed the skin of a successful CEO

309
00:26:24,105 --> 00:26:26,355
and just be my true self.

310
00:26:29,063 --> 00:26:33,855
Admitting your own weaknesses
is the first step to treating addiction.

311
00:26:34,730 --> 00:26:38,438
Why don't you try sharing
those feelings with your wife?

312
00:26:38,521 --> 00:26:40,271
I can't do that.

313
00:26:40,896 --> 00:26:45,230
If I could, I'd like to get it
all off my chest and feel better.

314
00:26:48,480 --> 00:26:50,813
But she wouldn't listen to any of this.

315
00:26:51,563 --> 00:26:52,855
I told you, didn't I?

316
00:26:53,688 --> 00:26:55,938
She tunes me out
whenever I try to talk to her.

317
00:27:00,438 --> 00:27:01,813
The other day,

318
00:27:03,188 --> 00:27:05,605
I suddenly remembered something
on my way home.

319
00:27:07,563 --> 00:27:09,771
The day I decided to get married.

320
00:27:11,021 --> 00:27:14,063
I'd started a company,
but it was going nowhere.

321
00:27:16,230 --> 00:27:18,771
I was running out of savings too.

322
00:27:19,271 --> 00:27:20,563
I'm sorry.

323
00:27:21,896 --> 00:27:25,063
You don't wanna marry
a guy like me, right?

324
00:27:25,146 --> 00:27:28,396
<i>I wasn't sure whether I should get married</i>
<i>when my life was so unstable,</i>

325
00:27:28,480 --> 00:27:31,271
<i>or whether I could provide for her.</i>

326
00:27:31,771 --> 00:27:34,980
You don't wanna marry
a guy like me, right?

327
00:27:35,063 --> 00:27:36,480
<i>When I let my doubts slip…</i>

328
00:27:37,396 --> 00:27:40,355
I never asked you to provide for me.

329
00:27:44,646 --> 00:27:45,480
Huh?

330
00:27:45,563 --> 00:27:48,646
Why does marriage mean providing for me?

331
00:27:48,730 --> 00:27:51,146
I can earn my own living.

332
00:27:53,105 --> 00:27:56,355
Don't get me wrong.
I'm not saying I'll provide for <i>you</i>.

333
00:27:58,021 --> 00:28:00,355
I know that!

334
00:28:01,563 --> 00:28:04,771
That made me so happy.

335
00:28:06,313 --> 00:28:08,063
If you still remember that,

336
00:28:09,980 --> 00:28:12,271
why are you still doing things
you don't want to?

337
00:28:14,063 --> 00:28:14,896
What?

338
00:28:16,771 --> 00:28:20,771
I'm asking why you're settling
for a life you don't want!

339
00:28:47,438 --> 00:28:48,646
Wait!

340
00:28:49,146 --> 00:28:50,313
No!

341
00:28:50,396 --> 00:28:51,855
I said wait!

342
00:28:58,480 --> 00:28:59,980
Stop running away!

343
00:29:00,063 --> 00:29:01,230
No!

344
00:29:03,688 --> 00:29:04,521
Huh?

345
00:29:05,355 --> 00:29:07,480
Listen to me!

346
00:29:08,855 --> 00:29:10,063
No!

347
00:29:10,146 --> 00:29:12,313
I can't do this!

348
00:29:13,980 --> 00:29:16,563
You're the one who never listened to me!

349
00:29:50,896 --> 00:29:54,563
I didn't listen because I already knew

350
00:29:54,646 --> 00:29:57,730
<i>what was coming after your "hey."</i>

351
00:29:59,480 --> 00:30:01,271
<i>I could tell if it was about your dreams</i>

352
00:30:03,396 --> 00:30:05,480
<i>or just another complaint.</i>

353
00:30:07,480 --> 00:30:10,646
I've had enough of that dead-eyed "hey."

354
00:30:13,521 --> 00:30:14,896
But as the CEO, I--

355
00:30:14,980 --> 00:30:16,438
<i>Did you want to become a CEO?</i>

356
00:30:17,021 --> 00:30:18,313
You didn't, right?

357
00:30:18,396 --> 00:30:22,730
Didn't you want to create a service
that would make people's lives easier?

358
00:30:22,813 --> 00:30:24,855
So you're saying you'd be fine with me

359
00:30:25,730 --> 00:30:27,771
quitting as CEO and becoming poor again?

360
00:30:27,855 --> 00:30:30,313
Didn't you like living in luxury?

361
00:30:30,396 --> 00:30:31,980
<i>Dressing up, going to parties…</i>

362
00:30:32,063 --> 00:30:34,313
You're so stupid!

363
00:30:34,813 --> 00:30:37,105
That was networking. And you're bad at it!

364
00:30:38,480 --> 00:30:41,146
<i>A grumpy-faced CEO</i>
<i>makes everyone else feel uneasy.</i>

365
00:30:41,230 --> 00:30:44,438
<i>Do you know how hard I've worked</i>
<i>to keep the mood up?</i>

366
00:30:45,521 --> 00:30:49,230
I'd feel a lot better
if I didn't have to do that anymore!

367
00:30:59,063 --> 00:31:01,021
You're really okay with me quitting?

368
00:31:02,938 --> 00:31:06,605
There's a service I've wanted to build,
but no one else is on board.

369
00:31:07,771 --> 00:31:08,980
Go ahead.

370
00:31:10,813 --> 00:31:13,355
Go make your spy code again.

371
00:31:14,605 --> 00:31:16,021
<i>But in return,</i>

372
00:31:17,105 --> 00:31:21,605
<i>I want you to tell me about your dreams</i>
<i>with that sparkle in your eyes again.</i>

373
00:31:35,438 --> 00:31:36,646
I knew.

374
00:31:39,271 --> 00:31:42,105
I knew you were into this kind of thing.

375
00:31:53,188 --> 00:31:54,813
<i>I was shocked,</i>

376
00:31:56,938 --> 00:31:59,146
but trying it now, it's not so bad.

377
00:32:01,563 --> 00:32:04,355
That avatar suits you.

378
00:32:10,396 --> 00:32:12,730
I should've talked to you sooner.

379
00:32:15,355 --> 00:32:17,230
You can say that again!

380
00:32:19,813 --> 00:32:22,521
I'm really sorry.

381
00:33:02,355 --> 00:33:03,938
Thank you very much.

382
00:33:18,605 --> 00:33:21,855
You were a great help, Saikawa.

383
00:33:22,563 --> 00:33:23,521
Huh?

384
00:33:24,480 --> 00:33:28,021
I almost got her hurt.

385
00:33:29,646 --> 00:33:30,730
Thank you.

386
00:33:33,146 --> 00:33:36,688
Well, I think I'm more athletic
than you, Doctor.

387
00:33:38,813 --> 00:33:40,438
Why?

388
00:33:40,521 --> 00:33:42,563
Why'd you give them to her?

389
00:33:42,646 --> 00:33:45,021
Those goggles and sensors were expensive!

390
00:33:45,105 --> 00:33:46,480
We don't need them anymore.

391
00:33:46,563 --> 00:33:47,980
If you didn't need them,

392
00:33:48,688 --> 00:33:51,230
we could've sold them online!

393
00:33:51,813 --> 00:33:53,230
You'd better get us a donation!

394
00:33:53,313 --> 00:33:55,396
He said he's stepping down as CEO,

395
00:33:55,480 --> 00:33:57,688
so money might be tight
for him for a while.

396
00:33:57,771 --> 00:33:58,605
Right?

397
00:33:59,313 --> 00:34:00,938
-What?
-Yes.

398
00:34:04,355 --> 00:34:06,438
What's the plan for his treatment?

399
00:34:07,271 --> 00:34:08,730
Of course, we'll continue.

400
00:34:09,230 --> 00:34:13,313
But I don't think he needs to stop
virtual sex altogether

401
00:34:14,855 --> 00:34:17,021
<i>as long as he maintains</i>
<i>healthy boundaries.</i>

402
00:34:18,313 --> 00:34:22,271
<i>So I had him promise</i>
<i>to only use it with his wife.</i>

403
00:34:23,688 --> 00:34:28,230
<i>Sex involves both</i>
<i>physical and emotional pleasure.</i>

404
00:34:30,063 --> 00:34:33,688
<i>And virtual sex,</i>
<i>which focuses on the emotional side,</i>

405
00:34:35,313 --> 00:34:40,146
<i>may help them reconnect.</i>

406
00:34:43,480 --> 00:34:45,188
What's important is

407
00:34:46,146 --> 00:34:48,605
acknowledging your weaknesses…

408
00:34:53,855 --> 00:34:56,771
and being honest about how you feel.

409
00:35:06,021 --> 00:35:07,438
SUSHI YUKIAKARI

410
00:35:11,688 --> 00:35:12,896
Ichinose.

411
00:35:22,563 --> 00:35:24,771
Sorry. I surprised you, didn't I?

412
00:35:25,896 --> 00:35:26,896
No.

413
00:35:28,396 --> 00:35:30,355
Actually, yeah, you did.

414
00:35:35,146 --> 00:35:37,771
About the other day…

415
00:35:45,438 --> 00:35:49,438
It's not that I was rejecting you.

416
00:36:13,480 --> 00:36:14,480
I…

417
00:36:18,271 --> 00:36:19,938
I can't have sex.

418
00:36:22,563 --> 00:36:24,355
-What?
-So…

419
00:36:24,438 --> 00:36:27,980
I wanted you to know that
the problem was with me that night.

420
00:36:41,521 --> 00:36:43,355
I like you.

421
00:36:47,230 --> 00:36:48,230
Will you

422
00:36:49,188 --> 00:36:50,813
go out with me?

423
